---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Roost"
  description="Terms for using the Roost managed dashboard beta service."
>
  <section class="section legal-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          These terms apply when you create an account or use the Roost managed dashboard service.
        </p>
        <p class="updated">Last updated August 31, 2026</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose">
        <h2>Free beta service</h2>
        <p>
          Roost is currently offered as a free beta. Features, limits, and availability may change as the service is
          developed. There is no promise that the beta will remain free or continue indefinitely. If paid service is
          introduced, you will be given notice and a choice before being charged.
        </p>

        <h2>Your account and devices</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for providing accurate account information, keeping control of your email account,
          password, and authorized devices, and for activity performed through your account. Use a strong, unique
          password if you add one. Promptly revoke a lost or untrusted device and contact
          <a href="mailto:support@roosttt.com">support@roosttt.com</a> if you suspect unauthorized access.
        </p>
        <p>
          Capacity is limited during the beta. New account creation may be paused or refused when the service is full,
          even if signup is otherwise available. One person may not evade account, identity, rate, storage, or capacity
          limits by creating or coordinating additional accounts.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You may not use Roost to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>break the law or violate another person’s rights;</li>
          <li>access or attempt to access an account, device, system, or data without authorization;</li>
          <li>distribute malware, facilitate phishing or spam, or operate abusive automated traffic;</li>
          <li>probe, bypass, or interfere with authentication, rate limits, isolation, network controls, or security;</li>
          <li>disrupt the service or impose unreasonable load on shared infrastructure; or</li>
          <li>use service content or access to harass, exploit, or harm others.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Good-faith security reports are welcome at
          <a href="mailto:support@roosttt.com">support@roosttt.com</a>. Do not access another user’s data or degrade the
          service while testing a report.
        </p>

        <h2>Your content</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of content you submit to Roost and are responsible for having the right to use it. You
          give Roost permission to process, transmit, store, and back up that content only as needed to provide,
          secure, and support the service. Do not submit content that these terms prohibit.
        </p>
        <p>
          Roost’s backups are operational recovery material, not a guaranteed archival service. Keep an independent
          copy of anything you cannot afford to lose.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          Roost may be unavailable because of maintenance, failures, provider outages, security incidents, or capacity
          constraints. Features may be added, changed, limited, or removed. Roost does not promise uninterrupted,
          error-free, or permanent access, any particular uptime, or recovery of all content.
        </p>

        <h2>Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>
          Access may be limited, suspended, or disabled to address abuse, a security risk, legal requirements,
          noncompliance with these terms, capacity or operational emergencies, or harm to Roost or others. When it is
          reasonable and safe, Roost will try to explain the action. You may stop using the service at any time and may
          contact support to request account deletion. Disabling an account does not by itself delete its data; see the
          <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for current retention details.
        </p>

        <h2>Open-source software and hosted service</h2>
        <p>
          The Roost source code published at
          <a href="https://github.com/cefege/roost" rel="noopener">github.com/cefege/roost</a> is licensed under the
          <a href="https://github.com/cefege/roost/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noopener">GNU General Public License v3.0
          only</a>. That license governs your use, copying, modification, and distribution of the published software.
        </p>
        <p>
          These terms separately govern access to the managed service at Roost-operated domains and infrastructure.
          The GPL license for the source code does not grant an account, hosted capacity, support entitlement, rights
          to Roost-operated domains or provider accounts, or permission to misuse the managed service.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranties</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by law, the free beta is provided <strong>“as is”</strong> and
          <strong>“as available”</strong>, without warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
          non-infringement, availability, security, or data preservation. You use the service at your own risk.
        </p>

        <h2>Limits of responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by law, Roost and its operator will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost data, profits, revenue, business, or opportunity
          arising from the beta service. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot legally be excluded.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes and support</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may be updated as the beta develops. The date above will be updated when they change. Continued
          use after an update means you accept the revised terms; if you do not agree, stop using the managed service.
          For support or questions about these terms, email
          <a href="mailto:support@roosttt.com">support@roosttt.com</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: var(--md-space-8);
  }

  .legal-header {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--md-space-8);
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--md-space-3);
    font-size: var(--md-headline-l-size);
    line-height: var(--md-headline-l-line);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: var(--md-space-4);
    color: var(--text-lo);
    font-size: var(--md-body-m-size);
    line-height: var(--md-body-m-line);
  }
</style>
